\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark, my soul! It is the Lord;
\par 'This thy Salvation, hear His word;
\par Jesus speaks, and speaks to thee:
\par Say, poor sinner, lov'st thou Me?
\par   
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I delivered thee when bound,
\par And, when bleeding, healed thy wound;
\par Sought thee wandering, set thee
\par Turned thy darkness in to light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Can a woman's tender care
\par Cease toward the child she bare?
\par Yes, she may forgetful be;
\par Yet will I remember thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Mine is an unchanging love,
\par Higher than the heights above,
\par Deeper than the depths beneath,
\par Free and faithful, strong as death
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thou shalt see my glory soon,
\par When the work of grace is done;
\par Partner of My throne shalt be;
\par Say, poor sinner, lov'st thou Me?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Lord, it is my chief complaint
\par That my love is weak and faint;
\par Yet I love Thee, and adore;
\par O for grace to love Thee more. 
\par                                  Amen.
\par  
\par  
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
